morgan: Quick note — customer hit Vercel edge size limit because our SDK pulled in `undici`. Need a tiny README snippet and a runnable shim pattern for ESM/CJS + TS. Anyone have a one-file pattern?

ran: Keep it small: prefer injected fetch, fall back to globalThis.fetch, then lazily import undici. Do not top-level import undici. Example: 
```js
// fetch-provider.js
export function makeFetch(override) {
  return async function fetcher(input, init) {
    if (override) return override(input, init);
    if (globalThis.fetch) return globalThis.fetch(input, init);
    try { const { fetch } = await import('undici'); return fetch(input, init); }
    catch (e) { throw new Error('No fetch available. Install undici or pass fetch() to makeFetch.'); }
  }
}
```

sam: Packaging rules: ship both ESM and CJS via conditional exports and add a tiny `fetch-shim` entry that points to an ESM module that only references globalThis.fetch. This lets bundlers pick the shim for browser/edge targets. Also mark `undici` optionalDependency so it isn't forced into installs.

morgan: Types — TS projects without DOM lib hit missing types. We should ship minimal ambient types in `types/fetch.d.ts` and point `types` in package.json. Example minimal types: 
```ts
// types/fetch.d.ts
export type FetchLike = (input: string | URL, init?: any) => Promise<any>;
export default FetchLike;
```
Document: prefer adding "DOM" to tsconfig lib for full types.

ci-bot: Added pipeline job `edge-bundle-scan` to detect `undici` in edge artifacts on PRs.

doc-bot: I'll draft the README snippet: 3 recipes (edge, node18+, node14/16) + troubleshooting FAQ. Will PR with examples and the minimal types.

morgan: great, please also include a short sentence telling CJS consumers to `await` the factory since it may async-load undici. That avoids weird require-time errors. Thanks! :thumbsup:
